=================================
LTS (Longturn Traditional Short) Ruleset for Freeciv21
=================================


OBJECTIVES:
-----------

- LTS is a short version of the LTT (Longturn Traditional) ruleset. A game
  is designed to be played through in roughly 40 turns: Space Flight should
  be reachable around turn 40 for a player who researches most of the tree.

- The tech tree, the unit list and the building list have been cut down
  heavily compared to LTT. Many balance values (unit and building costs,
  combat values, empire size, Roads wonders, airports, port facilities,
  partisans) have been imported from the Royale ruleset.

- Cities grow and produce very fast from the start, so the early game is
  short and the focus moves quickly to expansion, wonders and war.

- Everything not described here works as in LTT / civ2civ3. The in-game
  help is always the most accurate reference.


CORE RULES AT A GLANCE:
-----------------------

- City center tile: every city center gets +20 Food, +20 Shields and
  +20 Trade (plus the usual +1 Shield). Note that the Despotism/Tribal/
  Anarchy -1 penalty for tiles producing more than 2 also applies to the
  city center, Supermarket multiplies the extra food, and pollution on the
  center tile reduces the bonus.

- Granary size is 20 food for city sizes 1-4, then 24, 28, 34 and 40 for
  sizes 5, 6, 7 and 8+.

- Settlers cost 20 shields and 1 population, move 2 and ignore terrain
  (IgTer, like Alpine Troops): every step costs at most 1/3 move, so they
  travel 6 tiles per turn over any terrain. Railroads and maglevs are
  still faster.

- Settlers can only be built in the city with the Colonial Office (a small
  wonder, cost 20). Your first city gets the Colonial Office for free
  together with the Palace. You can move it by rebuilding it elsewhere,
  and if the city is lost a new one is placed in another of your cities.
  Because Settlers cost population, at most one Settlers can be built per
  turn and the city must be at least size 2.

- The Colonial Office becomes obsolete in 1920 AD (turn 25). Settlers
  can still be built on turn 24 (completed at the end of that turn).
  From turn 25 on they can no longer be put into production, but
  existing Settlers can still be used.

- Trade routes can only be established between the capitals (Palace
  cities) of different nations. Each capital has 4 trade route slots.
  Routes are bidirectional and give only ongoing trade: there is no
  one-time bonus. If either city stops being a capital (Palace moved or
  city lost), the route is cancelled at the next turn change.

- Pollution is halved compared to standard rules. A Recycling Center
  (Engineering) removes 75% of the remaining pollution of its city.
  There is no global warming. Nuclear winter from fallout still exists.

- Tech leakage is 150% (server setting): techs already known by other
  players become much cheaper.

- Automatic free upgrades of obsolete units grow with the game turn
  (see UNIT UPGRADES below).


CALENDAR:
---------

The game starts in 4500 BC. Year 0 is skipped.

TURNS      YEARS/TURN   YEAR AT START OF TURN
1 - 10     500          T1 4500 BC ... T10 1 AD
10 - 14    250          T11 250, T12 500, T13 750, T14 1000
14 - 16    300          T15 1300, T16 1600
16 - 21    40           T20 1760, T21 1800
21 - 26    30           T26 1950
26 - 31    10           T31 2000
31 - 36    5            T36 2025
36 -       1            2026, 2027, ...

There are no timeline slowdown effects, so the space race does not change
the calendar.


UNIT UPGRADES:
--------------

Every player gets free upgrades of obsolete units every turn, starting
from the turn change at the end of turn 4:

FROM TURN   UPGRADES PER TURN
4           1
8           2
12          4
16          6
20          8

These add up with other upgrade effects:
- Tactics known by any player: +2 per turn for everybody.
- Radio known by any player: +2 per turn for everybody.
- Leonardo's Workshop: +2 per turn for the owner.
- Verrocchio's Workshop: +1 per turn for the owner.

Invention makes paid upgrades 20% cheaper, Computers another 30% (50% in
total).


SCIENCE AND TECHS:
------------------

- 33 techs. Costs are the values below multiplied by 3 (Tech_Cost_Factor),
  before tech leakage and the sciencebox server setting.
- Techs without a listed cost use the Classic formula (about 14 before the
  x3 factor; Construction about 40).

TECH               REQUIRES                          COST   IN GAME
Bronze Working     -                                 -      ~42
Ceremonial Burial  -                                 -      ~42
Pottery            -                                 -      ~42
Warrior Code       -                                 -      ~42
Construction       Warrior Code, Pottery             -      ~120
Writing            Ceremonial Burial                 25     75
Trade              Ceremonial Burial, Bronze Working 30     90
Seafaring          Pottery                           40     120
Feudalism          Writing, Trade                    60     180
Banking            Trade                             60     180
University         Writing, Construction             70     210
Gunpowder          Construction, Writing             90     270
Economics          Feudalism, Banking                110    330
Democracy          Banking, Writing                  110    330
Navigation         Construction, Seafaring           220    660
Invention          Navigation, University            240    720
Railroad           Construction, Banking             240    720
Tactics            Gunpowder, Feudalism              260    780
Electricity        Gunpowder, University             280    840
Electronics        Economics                         300    900
Engineering        Electricity, Invention            320    960
Industrialization  Railroad, Banking                 350    1050
Combustion         Industrialization, Engineering    380    1140
Mass Production    Industrialization, Economics      450    1350
Flight             Combustion, Tactics               540    1620
Automobile         Mass Production, Combustion       600    1800
Computers          Electronics, Engineering          620    1860
Radio              Flight, Electronics               660    1980
Nuclear Fission    Electronics                       720    2160
Rocketry           Flight                            780    2340
Combined Arms      Tactics, Flight                   780    2340
Space Flight       Computers, Rocketry               1080   3240
Fusion Power       Space Flight, Nuclear Fission     2500   7500

Special tech effects:

- Construction: forts and fortresses; roads and railroads on river tiles
  (bridges).
- Trade: +30% shields in all your cities; halves production waste by
  distance.
- University: +30% shields in all your cities; works as Barracks in all
  your cities (new military land units, including siege units, are
  veterans; land units staying a full turn in a city are fully restored);
  doubles the Temple effect (not under Communism); fortress watchtowers.
- Democracy: when any player knows it, all players get the road trade
  bonus (+1 trade on Desert, Grassland, Plains and Tundra) even without a
  road. Allows Barracks.
- Railroad: when any player knows it, every tile that could be irrigated
  (and has no mine) gets the irrigation bonus automatically for all
  players. Hand-built irrigation is then only needed for Farmland. Also
  cancels the Despotism/Tribal tile penalty.
- Electricity: irrigation without a water source, better Amphitheaters,
  larger city vision.
- Engineering: allows building Nuclear units (see NUCLEAR WEAPONS).
- Invention: paid unit upgrades 20% cheaper.
- Computers: paid unit upgrades another 30% cheaper; maglev; oil platforms
  on deep ocean; mining on deep ocean; Offshore Platform.
- Electronics: Farmland, Supermarket, Power Plant.
- Combustion: Oil Wells on desert and glacier mines.
- Automobile: +50% shields in all your cities.
- Radio: +9 movement for Nuclear units; when any player knows it, +2 free
  unit upgrades per turn for everybody.
- Tactics: partisans (see UNITS); when any player knows it, +2 free unit
  upgrades per turn for everybody.
- Fusion Power: +50% shields in all your cities.

All shield percentages add up with each other and with Factory and Power
Plant (for example Trade + University + Automobile + Fusion Power = +160%).


GOVERNMENTS:
------------

GOVERNMENT      TECH               MAX RATE  CORRUPTION  WASTE  EMPIRE BASE/STEP
Anarchy         -                  100 (*)   -           30%    -
Tribal          -                  60        30%         0%     7 / 4
Despotism       -                  60        20%         10%    5 / 3
Monarchy        Ceremonial Burial  70        10%         10%    10 / 5
Fundamentalism  Feudalism          60        15%         15%    10 / 6
Republic        University         80        25%         20%    8 / 5
Federation      Economics          90        0% (**)     30%    10 / 6
Democracy       Democracy          90        5%          25%    6 / 3
Communism       Industrialization  80        30% (***)   0%     10 / 7

(*)   Anarchy has no control over the budget: half of the trade is lost and
      the rest goes to luxuries.
(**)  Federation corruption grows only with distance (half as fast), and
      Mass Production removes it.
(***) Communism corruption is not affected by distance.

- Corruption and waste increase with distance from the capital. Mass
  Production halves the corruption by distance, Trade halves the
  production waste by distance.
- Empire size: the base is the number of cities you can have before every
  city gets one extra unhappy citizen; after that one more unhappy
  citizen is added every "step" cities. These values are half of the
  Royale base values, with the Royale steps.
- Free units per city: Anarchy 2, Tribal 2, Despotism 2, Monarchy 3,
  Fundamentalism 2, Republic 2, Democracy 1, Federation 2, Communism 3.
  The number of free units is doubled for cities of size 9 or more.
- Monarchy is available almost immediately, so Tribal and Despotism are
  mostly short opening governments.
- The Statue of Liberty (Democracy) allows choosing any government.


