Military unit costs and combat values follow the Royale ruleset.

Upgrade paths:
- Warriors -> Phalanx -> Musketeers -> Infantry; Archers -> Musketeers
- Horsemen -> Knights -> Cavalry
- Cannon -> Howitzer
- Longboat -> Caravel -> Galleon -> Transport; Frigate -> Destroyer
- Fighter -> Stealth Fighter; Bomber -> Stealth Bomber
- Workers -> Engineers; Diplomat -> Spy; Caravan -> Freight

Special unit rules:

- Settlers: see CORE RULES. They also count as terrain workers.

- Partisans cannot be built. When an enemy conquers your city, a number
  of Partisans appear around it if you know Tactics, your government is
  Monarchy, Communism, Fundamentalism, Federation, Republic or Democracy,
  and at least 75% of the citizens have your nationality.

- Submarines: need a Port Facility, which needs your own Electricity and
  Combustion known by any player. Submarines can carry missiles.

- Aircraft: all planes need an Airport, which needs your own Combustion
  and Flight known by any player. Fighters therefore only need
  Combustion.

- Galleon (Navigation) is the first ship that can carry Big Land and
  siege units (Armor, Cannon, Howitzer).

- Caravan and Freight can establish trade routes between capitals (see
  CORE RULES) and help build wonders.

- Cruise Missile has no home city.


NUCLEAR WEAPONS:
----------------

- Nuclear units can be built by anyone who knows Engineering.
- They can be moved freely, but nobody can detonate them before the
  Manhattan Project (Nuclear Fission, cost 600) has been built by any
  player. After that, every player can detonate their Nuclear units, even
  if the wonder is later destroyed ("balance of terror").
- Nuclear units have 9 movement points, 18 with Radio. They can be
  carried by Submarines and Carriers.
- SDI Defense (Electricity) shoots down 75% of foreign nuclear attacks,
  100% in the Palace city.


TERRAIN AND TILES:
------------------

- Roads give +1 trade on Desert, Grassland, Plains and Tundra. Once any
  player knows Democracy, those tiles get the bonus without a road.
- Once any player knows Railroad, all irrigable tiles without a mine get
  the irrigation bonus automatically.
- Roads on river tiles need Construction.
- Oil Wells (Combustion) on desert and glacier mines; oil platforms on
  deep ocean (Computers) for Offshore Platforms.
- Farmland needs Electronics and an irrigated tile; Supermarket gives
  +50% food on Farmland.
- Maglev needs Computers.
- Other terrain values are as in LTT.


SERVER SETTINGS (LTS.serv):
---------------------------

- techleak 150
- spaceship_travel_time 100
- globalwarming disabled
- sciencebox 100, foodbox 100, shieldbox 100
- victories SPACERACE|ALLIED
- barbarians disabled, huts 0
- startunits cccccwwwwwwxx (5 Settlers, 6 Workers, 2 Explorers)

The sciencebox setting can be used to fine-tune the pace of the tech tree
without changing the ruleset.


REMOVED COMPARED TO LTT:
------------------------

Techs: Advanced Espionage, Advanced Flight, Alphabet, Amphibious Warfare,
Astronomy, Atomic Theory, Aviation Endurance, Bridge Building, Chemistry,
Chivalry, Code of Laws, Communism (tech), Conscription, Currency,
Environmentalism, Espionage, Explosives, Genetic Engineering, Guerilla
Warfare, Horseback Riding, Iron Working, Labor Union, Laser, Leadership,
Literacy, Machine Tools, Magnetism, Map Making, Masonry, Mathematics,
Medicine, Metallurgy, Miniaturization, Mobile Warfare, Monarchy (tech),
Monotheism, Mysticism, Nuclear Power, Philosophy, Physics, Plastics,
Polytheism, Recycling, Refining, Refrigeration, Robotics, Sanitation,
Stealth, Steam Engine, Steel, Superconductors, The Corporation, The
Republic (tech), The Wheel, Theology, Theory of Gravity.

Units: Immigrants, Swordsmen, Pikemen, Riflemen, Mech. Inf., Chariot,
Elephants, Crusaders, Dragoons, Catapult, Artillery, Trireme, Barge,
Square-Rigged Caravel, Flagship Frigate, Ironclad, Cruiser, Nuclear
Submarine, Missile, Intercontinental Missile, Nuclear Bomb, Operative,
Fusion Fighter, Fusion Bomber, Fusion Battleship, Fusion Armor, Cargo
Aircraft.

Buildings: Mercantile Exchange, Barracks II, Barracks III, Cathedral,
Hydro Plant, Mass Transit, Mfg. Plant, Nuclear Plant, Police Station,
Research Lab, Solar Plant, Super Highways, SDI Defense II and III (merged
into one SDI Defense).

Wonders: Colossus, Cure For Cancer, Darwin's Voyage, Eiffel Tower, Hoover
Dam, J.S. Bach's Cathedral, King Richard's Crusade, Magellan's Expedition,
Michelangelo's Chapel, Mausoleum of Mausolos, Statue of Zeus, Internet,
United Nations, Hal Saflieni Hypogeum, Sun Tzu's War Academy.

Added: Colonial Office, Silk Road, Gold Road, Gems Road, Ivory Road
(from Royale).


